  "notes": "SWV's architect: melodic R&B with a house/disco undertow, windowed 1992–1997 in this lane. The research gives \"63–99: ballads 63–74 half-time (backbeat on 3), uptempos 85–99 straight\", and the ballad band is the base with the mode at 63 — the published sheet for the signature record marks it **D minor at 63 BPM, \"slow groove\"**, and the entry says that notation is the parameter: \"his ballads are notated as grooves, not free ballads, which is the parameter that separates him from the Foster/Afanasieff school\". So this model is a half-time ballad that still *moves*: `fourOnFloorInChorus` is true (Martha Wash compared his work to Patrick Cowley's — a disco/house pulse under R&B), the hat runs continuous 16ths at 0.28 with open hats on both offbeats, and the perc bed is an offbeat shaker/tambourine/conga set at three to five hits a bar — none of which the section's other ballad producers carry. The two remaining drum deltas are quoted: \"a snare-roll pickup into the chorus\" (a `snareRoll` ladder with `pre_downbeat` roll positions) and \"a shaker on offbeat 8ths\". Harmony is \"4-chord minor cycles, added-9th pads, and **the top voice left free above the harmony for melisma**\", so ninth is 0.36 and the melody is authored wide: MIDI 62–92, a 0.56 arch weight and a 0.14 octave-jump probability, because \"he writes strong, wide melodies that force the singer out of habit\". The bass is \"rounded synth bass doubling the chord root with a short slide into the downbeat\", `[LOW-CONF]`, with \"house-derived octave motion on the up-tempos\" — hence the octave cell shapes. ⚠ Every velocity and density number is INFERRED. ⚠ `session.keys` is part-sourced: the entry names `Dm`, `Am`, and the remaining values `Bbm`, `Fm`, together with all 4 weights, are INFERRED rather than read from the entry.",
